# /sdd-update

Purpose:
  Synchronize .sdd/ state from git repository. Reads branch structure,
  commit history, and file changes to auto-update SDD metadata.

Description:
  Scans git repo to discover: current branch, recent commits, changed files,
  active modules, tasks, and decisions. Updates .sdd/ files to reflect
  actual repo state. Detects drift between code and specification.

Usage:
  /sdd-update
  /sdd-update --full
  /sdd-update --diff
  /sdd-update --modules
  /sdd-update --tasks

Options:
  --full      Full sync including all modules, tasks, decisions
  --diff      Show drift between .sdd/ and project/
  --modules   Sync module states only
  --tasks     Sync task states only

Behavior:
  1. Read git branch, recent commits, changed files
  2. Map commits to modules/tasks/decisions
  3. Update .sdd/ state symbols based on git evidence
  4. Detect orphaned .sdd entries (no matching code)
  5. Detect unrecorded code (no matching .sdd)
  6. Emit drift report
  7. Update INDEX.sdd references if needed

AutoMode:
  trigger: git post-commit, post-checkout, post-merge
  scope: incremental (affected modules/tasks only)
  mode: background, non-blocking
  fail: open (log drift, do not block workflow)

Output:
  [updated: modules=X, tasks=Y, decisions=Z]
  [drift: orphaned=N, unrecorded=M]
  [branch: main]
  [last_commit: abc1234]

Rules:
  [UPD-01] git state is source of truth for module/task completion.
  [UPD-02] Orphaned .sdd entries are flagged, not deleted.
  [UPD-03] Unrecorded code blocks Write|Edit hooks until documented.
  [UPD-04] Auto-update runs in background, never blocks human workflow.
  [UPD-05] Drift report is appended to .sdd/state/drift.log.sdd.

State: +
